## Course Objectives

(1) We will discuss the observed properties of galaxies, including the observational techniques that use to obtain those results; 

(2) We will discuss the theoretical components for forming galaxies in the cosmological context;

(3) We will discuss the open questions of galaxy evolution.

## Learning Outcomes

After this course,  

(1) Students know the underlying relationships between galaxy observables and the current understanding of the corresponding astrophysics;

(2) Students have a broad picture of galaxy evolution in general and understand how each sub-field connects to this broad picture;

(3) Students are able to understand the bulk of the galaxy-related talks;   

(4) Students are able to deliver oral presentations in a professional setting.

